      "sourceTextSha256": "d5b88741a04e786f132e59cde92030ed112c3b1868b145c94ca78d291cfd36e0",
      "text": "Day 7 · Semuc Champey, one of the most beautiful places in Guatemala: a natural limestone bridge, about 300 m long, beneath which the Cahabón River disappears, while above it a series of turquoise pools, from emerald green to sapphire blue, invites you to swim. Its Q’eqchi’ name means “where the river hides under the stones”. Another glamping night near Lanquín. (B)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1MfFMYvTkHizz2y7XQmdC0cIjNgd0tmbg",
